From dde54406896328b1a9c8ce10f1c11f81ba1c7c43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arthur Clark <mydevstuff@mail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/33] QNX: add a LibreOfficeKit render-regression gate

The upstream LOK render tests are unusable as a QNX discovery gate:
tiledrendering is disabled (tdf#113311) and its source no longer matches the
paintTile API, and smoketest pulls in the whole office application layer. This
standalone gate renders a 256x256 tile of each fixed input through
LibreOfficeKit and checks the non-white pixel count against a per-document band
- the floor rejects a blank tile, the ceiling rejects a garbage one - with a
malformed input carried as a negative control that must fail to render. rc=0 iff
every case meets its expectation.

Built native-on-QDD with clang++; links the UNO exception RTTI anchor with
--dynamic-list-cpp-typeinfo, without which the QNX executable-first loader
returns an empty documentLoad.

Change-Id: I4957c61c390cb7f039cb0c1464d017354d3f4ce8
